      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Inoculation of rats at the tail-base with Mycobacterium led to arthritic swelling and inflammation of all four limbs. Immunoreactive (ir)-dynorphin (DYN) increased in anterior but not neurointermediate pituitary. In the brain, only thalamus showed a rise and, in spinal cord, a large elevation was seen. Ir-vasopressin (VP) was not affected in these tissues but increased in midbrain. These effects might reflect a role of DYN in the control of chronic pain. In addition, they support a differential modulation of DYN as compared to VP extrinsic to the hypothalamic-neurohypophyseal axis."},
